// Regression for issue #388: a closure over a plain (non-self-recursive)
// local declared inside the try body that captures it, called only after
// the whole try/catch statement completes. Same root cause as #350's own
// self-recursion shape (examples/try_catch_self_recursive_closure.lox):
// the `catch (e)` clause's own SET_LOCAL used to read-before-write the
// slot it binds, to decide whether that slot already held a capture cell
// (isFreshDeclaration's own note in jvm_emitter.cpp), and the classic
// verifier assembling this backend's classes rejected that read as
// reachable before the captured local's slot was ever written --
// "VerifyError: Register N contains wrong type".

var fns = [];
try {
    var x = 41;
    fun c() { return x + 1; }
    fns.append(c);
} catch (e) { print e; }
print str(fns[0]());

// CHECK: 42
